body: "## Intent\n\nUse 100$ for the rest of the tasks, we need to enrich london data. Stick to tavily to extract whatever we can.\n\ndone continue\n\nis verythign working properly? Pls finish everything\n\nI am going to work , pls complete everyhting and you all the permissions\n\nI have credits, thats how you are running, just keep finishing the tasks\n\nuse the plugins , we have firecrawl so use the credits\n\nfinish the rest using GNHF\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Refresh London pub hours and dog-policy evidence, expanding source records from 299 to 369 and removing a generic chain dog statement.\n- Publish two Thirsty Bear cider pint prices and extend reconciliation records and regression coverage while preserving the historical withdrawal audit.\n- Add Firecrawl coverage snapshots, source decisions, review excerpts, credit accounting and local reader evidence, with documented publication limits.\n\n## Risk Assessment\n\n✅ Low: The bounded enrichment preserves existing hours schedules and price rows, retains source ownership and exclusions, and introduces no runtime subsystem.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe supplied baseline passed. A keyless production build, focused suites, live API checks, and desktop/mobile screenshots verified runtime delivery. Retained accounting reconciled, while the original cached-menu extraction remains untested.\n\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 7 of 8 scenarios driven live against the product\n\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Open enriched curated pubs and receive their source facts under the correct venue IDs. | ✅ pass | live | Kew Greyhound opening hours; Live detail responses and price preservation; Published source ownership |\n| Open Sydenham’s Greyhound and see Monday–Thursday hours while Friday–Sunday remain Not stated. | ✅ pass | live | Sydenham Greyhound unstated days |\n| Open Brixton Brewery Tap Room and see Dogs welcome with dated pub-website credit on desktop and mobile. | ✅ pass | live | Brixton dog policy on desktop; Brixton dog policy on mobile |\n| Open other Greyhound pubs and The Bull’s Head without receiving another pub’s facts or the withdrawn generic dog statement. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation; Generic chain dog-policy withdrawal |\n| Read existing venue details and the published bundle after merging, preserving all 297 baseline hours schedules and 7,595 previous price rows. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation |\n| Read the published price bundle and find only two additions: Inches Cider pint £5.95 and Whisky Cider pint £4.95. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation |\n| Open UK base pub records and retain their identities without presenting collected website hours as runtime coverage. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation |\n| Replay the original retained Thirsty Bear menu through the shared harvest reader and reproduce its accepted named pint rows. | ⏸️ untested | no | I replayed the committed five-line excerpt through both shared reader interfaces. It returned no publishable named drinks. The excerpt does not include the full retained input or preprocessing used by… |\n\n![Kew Greyhound opening hours](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b8097ae9-0d85-453c-911a-fad0666fc63e)\n![Sydenham Greyhound unstated days](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ec92be6c-d2e3-4fad-b43c-c32d97fdb17c)\n![Brixton dog policy on desktop](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/db663169-e357-494b-9b85-c5925f7ea7e8)\n![Brixton dog policy on mobile](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ef6bdeb-5b7a-48b5-97fa-6676e2d094e0)\n<details>\n<summary>Evidence: Live detail responses and price preservation</summary>\n\n```text\n{\n  \"root\": \"http://127.0.0.1:50643\",\n  \"commit\": \"41958b27d6ea67655af645326e8e04ada1f3b37b\",\n  \"checkedAt\": \"2026-10-10T23:48:28.848Z\",\n  \"sourceDetails\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"venue-112egvu\",\n      \"name