\n<summary>🔧 **Rebase** - 1 issue found → auto-fixed ✅</summary>\n\n- ⚠️ `data/amenities/london_pub_website_hours_dogs.json` - merge conflict rebasing onto origin/main\n\n🔧 Fix applied.\n✅ Re-checked - no issues remain.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Review** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Test** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n- Live validation: ✅ go - 7 of 8 scenarios driven live against the product\n\n| Scenario | Result | Live | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Open enriched curated pubs and receive their source facts under the correct venue IDs. | ✅ pass | live | Kew Greyhound opening hours; Live detail responses and price preservation; Published source ownership |\n| Open Sydenham’s Greyhound and see Monday–Thursday hours while Friday–Sunday remain Not stated. | ✅ pass | live | Sydenham Greyhound unstated days |\n| Open Brixton Brewery Tap Room and see Dogs welcome with dated pub-website credit on desktop and mobile. | ✅ pass | live | Brixton dog policy on desktop; Brixton dog policy on mobile |\n| Open other Greyhound pubs and The Bull’s Head without receiving another pub’s facts or the withdrawn generic dog statement. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation; Generic chain dog-policy withdrawal |\n| Read existing venue details and the published bundle after merging, preserving all 297 baseline hours schedules and 7,595 previous price rows. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation |\n| Read the published price bundle and find only two additions: Inches Cider pint £5.95 and Whisky Cider pint £4.95. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation |\n| Open UK base pub records and retain their identities without presenting collected website hours as runtime coverage. | ✅ pass | live | Live detail responses and price preservation |\n| Replay the original retained Thirsty Bear menu through the shared harvest reader and reproduce its accepted named pint rows. | ⏸️ untested | no | I replayed the committed five-line excerpt through both shared reader interfaces. It returned no publishable named drinks. The excerpt does not include the full retained input or preprocessing used by… |\n\n- `npm run verify:no-mistakes`\n- <code>Supplied baseline: `npm run verify:no-mistakes` passed before this phase; not rerun.</code>\n- <code>`node scripts/run-with-restored-next-env.mjs npm run build` with isolated `NEXT_DIST_DIR`, restored public data, and provider credentials removed.</code>\n- <code>`npm run start -- --port 50643 --hostname 127.0.0.1` against the isolated production build.</code>\n- <code>`node node_modules/vitest/vitest.mjs run __tests__/siteHarvestReconciliation.test.ts __tests__/ukPriceBundle.test.ts __tests__/ukPriceCrawl.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`.</code>\n- <code>`node .test-london/api-check.cjs`: live curated details, UK base records, lookalike boundaries, and served bundle comparisons.</code>\n- <code>`node .test-london/ownership.cjs`: live published ownership checks and preserved baseline tuples.</code>\n- <code>`npm run e2e:cli -- -s=london-enrichment`: opening details, expanding hours, checking dog policy, capturing screenshots, and resizing to 390×844.</code>\n- <code>`TYPESAFE_API_KEY= node --conditions=react-server --import tsx .test-london/contracts.mts`: retained accounting, refusals, historical reconciliation, and evidence hash checks.</code>\n- <code>`TYPESAFE_API_KEY= node --conditions=react-server --import tsx .test-london/reader-replay.mts`: diagnostic replay of the abbreviated committed excerpt.</code>\n- <code>Live `GET /api/venue/venue-1j8bjz9` confirmed the generic dog statement was withdrawn while hours remained.</code>\n- `Closed the test browser and server, removed disposable Chromium and generated build files, and confirmed a clean worktree.`\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Document** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Lint** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ **Push** - passed</summary>\n\n✅ No issues found.\n</details>\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/Singularityszn/codesmith/pubmax/pr/2084?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1794268972&installation_model_id=430946&pr_number=2084&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=Singularityszn%2Fpubmax&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FSingularityszn%2Fpubmax%2Fpull%2F2084&signature=ab6b04aa01d9922106dc677502f09be767bf5f19b92fded6df6f43b74fb54e9e\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need. Autofix is disabled.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->"
